    inShort: "In short: The Global Positioning System (GPS) determines your physical coordinates on Earth by calculating how long radio signals take to travel from at least four orbiting satellites to your receiver. By multiplying signal travel time by the speed of light and compensating for atomic clock drift and Einsteinian relativity, your device pinpoints your latitude, longitude, and elevation on the WGS 84 ellipsoid.",

