    seg1Title: "The Space Segment (Satellite Constellations)",
    seg1Desc: "The baseline GPS constellation consists of at least 24 operational satellites (typically 31 active) operating in Medium Earth Orbit (MEO) at an altitude of approximately 20,200 kilometers. The satellites are arranged across six orbital planes inclined at 55 degrees relative to the equator, completing two orbits per sidereal day. This geometric distribution guarantees that any point on Earth with an unobstructed sky view can receive signals from at least six to ten satellites simultaneously.",
