    pWgs84_2: "Under WGS 84, latitude measures degrees north or south of the Equator (-90° to +90°), while longitude measures degrees east or west of the Prime Meridian in Greenwich (-180° to +180°). Understanding how these angles translate into meters on the ground is covered in our detailed guide on latitude and longitude explained. When converting between systems like UTM grid coordinates or local national datums, consulting our coordinate reference and datum guide is essential.",

