        q: "How many satellites does a modern smartphone actually connect to?",
        a: "Modern smartphones feature multi-GNSS chipsets that simultaneously track US GPS, European Galileo, Russian GLONASS, and Chinese BeiDou constellations. Under an open sky, a dual-frequency phone often tracks 20 to 35 satellites at once, achieving 1 to 3 meter precision."
      },
      {
        q: "Does GPS continue to work when my device is in Airplane Mode?",
        a: "Yes. Airplane Mode disables cellular, Wi-Fi, and Bluetooth radios, but the passive GPS receiver chip remains fully functional on modern operating systems because it emits no electromagnetic radiation."
      }
